      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I recently reached to VRChat support with this issue, as I have personal and content creation accounts, and was wondering the implications of trying to verify both, this is the reply I got, posting it here so people have more official information (hope it is ok to post this):\n\n\"Hi there,\n\n \n\nThanks for reaching out with your questions!\n\n \n\nYou can only complete Age Verification on one VRChat account per form of ID. If you’ve already verified an account using a particular ID, attempting to use the same ID on another account will result in an error. If you’d like to verify a different account instead, you’ll first need to remove verification from the currently verified account. Alternatively, if you have access to a second valid form of government-issued ID that is still yours, you can use that to verify a different account.\n\n \n\nPlease note that Age Verification does not publicly link or reveal any personal information across accounts, your identity will remain private and unassociated between accounts.\n\n \n\nAs for VRC+ subscriptions through Steam: a Steam account can only have one active VRChat account tied to its subscription at a time. The subscription doesn’t automatically link or associate any other accounts you may own, and it won’t cause any cross-account exposure.\n\nLilith\n\nVRChat Team\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
