      "value": "@{6449f7223e816f16885c76e2|full_name} I guess that the process Persona uses generates a unique token for the specific ID document, so different documents generate different tokens... Maybe, not sure. \n\nThe way I understand it, you could use your government ID, driver's license and passport to verify 3 accounts, for example, depending on what your country considers a valid ID.\n\nI would ask then if a specific type of ID is valid before trying, though.",
